A||N||3||DaveL||Door Striker Question||||1||
Z||000000||DaveL||03-21-2000||03:46 PM||||I have an 87 SE 2.5 DIS with 130,000 or so on it. I've noticed latelt that when I hit any fairly good bumps, both doors sound like they are rattling up and down. The old days, all GM strikers had clear plastic rings around them that would cause this type of rattle when they wore out. The striker posts on mine have nothing like that, they are solid metal. I went down to the local GM dealer who pulled out a new one for me, and it didn't have this ring either. Was this done away with?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-21-2000||07:53 PM||||I have the same problem. same latches.<P>The normal fix was to adjust and rotate such a strike. Problem is GM zeroed the damn hole so there is no adjustment. The actual problem isn't so much that the strick is worn. the lathch in the door is worn, and even a new strike can't be adjusted to compensate. As soon as I get some good weather I'm going to have a better look at it. It's annoying as hell.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||03-21-2000||08:03 PM||||Ah, the typical Fiero rattling door. With my 87 SE it was a combination of worn hinge pins and worn striker/latch. My striker was adjustable and I mentioned that last summer, but got a couple emails correcting me. Apparently not all Fieros have an adjustable striker as Ogre mentioned. Open up the door halfway and see if there is up and down movement which indicates worn hinge pins. If the pins are worn, the striker will have a flat spot wore down on the topside.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIEROCIOUS||03-21-2000||10:28 PM||||I have had and since corrected this problem! If you can't move the door up and down and feel movement in the hinges It's the mechanism on the door it's self!<P>I bought from a junk yard the lock due hicky from a newer 90's buick or some other luxury car by GM. Make sure It's the same latch system. The latch on the rear of a four door can not be used, they have no provision for a key lock. <P>The neatest thing is the newer ones have a spring that pops the door out for you when you open the door. Kinda like you pull the handle and pop it's open, no pushing out while pulling the handle! I would recomend doing this for only this reason!<P><BR>Mike||||reg||1
